1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:21,622
Rusk arrived at breakfast wearing a pistol that had apparently charged
him rent for the entire right side of his body. He approached his
chair sideways. Tank watched him try to sit. "Nigga, who wearing who?"
"I have never worn one before." "We can see the relationship
developing." Rosa moved the fruit bowl out of the struggle.

2
00:00:21,872 --> 00:00:48,012
Rusk finally settled beside Marcellus and laid a rolled banner across
the table. "Fourteen houses," he said. "Three more before dawn. The
horse appears to have persuaded them." "Nigga, that horse got more
votes than some governments," Tank said. Two officers brought the
other end through the doorway. An officer turned. The cloth caught the
lamp. Rosa caught the lamp. Tank caught the officer.

3
00:00:48,262 --> 00:01:08,629
"Nigga, stop. Everybody stop acquiring objects." We stood still until
the room had its proper number of upright things. Then Rusk unrolled
my name. CAPTAIN AIDEN. FINAL CLAIMANT OF THE WEST. It crossed the
table, swallowed the bread basket, and kept coming. "Nigga, that's not
my name.

4
00:01:08,879 --> 00:01:33,502
That's a road closure." "The pledged houses appear beneath it." "They
paying by the letter?" One officer ducked under the cloth and came up
holding breakfast like he'd found survivors. Shawna took the plate
from him. "Thank you. My husband gets difficult without those."
"Without houses?" the officer asked. "Croissants, baby. The houses
will wait." Nigga, I married an expert.

5
00:01:33,752 --> 00:01:57,565
Rusk tried to read the pledges. Tank lifted the far edge, which pulled
the near edge over Rusk's head. The lord continued reading for another
four words before accepting that he could no longer see the document.
"Captain. Some assistance." "Nigga drowning in my reputation." Shawna
put a croissant in my mouth and pointed at the cloth. I took the other
end.

6
00:01:57,815 --> 00:02:17,255
Now we could see Orsini. Magnus. Laurent. Fourteen households standing
together where Zero had trained them to stand apart. The joke settled
a little in my hands. That was a lot of people to promise something
to. One officer pointed out his family's district near the bottom.

7
00:02:17,505 --> 00:02:38,698
"My captain says you've done more in a week than the court did in
twenty years." "Nigga, don't start measuring productivity. They'll
give me a desk." "A larger desk," Rusk said. Tank nodded toward the
banner. "Nigga needs a warehouse with a drawer." We folded it back
carefully this time. Nobody's name went under a plate.

8
00:02:38,948 --> 00:03:03,400
Shawna studied the available wall like she was already rearranging her
opera house to fit fourteen sets of expectations and one ridiculous
husband. "I told you the horse needed a stable," she said. "Baby,
apparently the nigga needs an embassy." Rusk didn't laugh. Nigga, that
made me put the coffee down. I could joke with a nervous nigga. I
could make a proud nigga laugh.

9
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:28,786
This nigga looked like somebody had reached into his house while he
was still trying to decide which jacket to wear. "What happened?" He
turned the banner over. On the back was a second instruction, written
in black. The final claim would proceed under armed imperial
supervision. No private household guards. No police inside the arena.
No substitution of a claimant's prize.

10
00:03:29,036 --> 00:03:51,365
The winner would attend the yacht coronation alone. "Nigga added
alone," Tank said. "He knows we found the book," I told them. Rusk's
mouth tightened. "He ordered me to record your voluntary acceptance."
"Did you?" "No." One little word again, and this nigga had finally
said it. Nigga, I watched his shoulders settle after it left his
mouth.

11
00:03:51,615 --> 00:04:12,372
The man looked like he had been carrying somebody else's ugly
furniture on his back and just put the whole damn room down. This city
kept making people work hard to say it. Rusk reached into his jacket
and took out his silver ceremonial chain. He set it beside the banner.
"I have served this tournament for twenty-two years.

12
00:04:12,622 --> 00:04:34,540
I have announced men I feared, praised men I despised, and made death
sound dignified because someone handed me the correct wording. Last
night my wife asked why I came home with blood on my cuffs. I told her
a man had saved me. She asked why I still worked for the man who sent
the killers." Nobody interrupted.

13
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:56,212
"I found I had no answer that would let me sleep beside her." I looked
at the chain. Then at him. "Nigga, keep that. You earned it doing the
wrong job long enough. Now do the right one with the same nice
jewelry." He laughed once, surprised. "What would you have me
announce?" Shawna slid a sheet of paper toward him. "A public final.

14
00:04:56,462 --> 00:05:21,775
Crown on the stage. Prizes awarded there. All houses present." "The
emperor will refuse." "Then announce that too," she said. We went to
House Orsini before noon. The old king met us in a courtyard full of
lemon trees. His wife, Leonora, sat beside a fountain feeding pieces
of pastry to a dog small enough to look like it had been assembled
from leftover pride.

15
00:05:22,025 --> 00:05:44,638
"The emperor wants your winner alone," I said. Lord Orsini sighed. "He
has always preferred private celebrations." "Nigga, you knew?" The old
man looked at me. For once, he didn't have a joke ready. Leonora
stopped feeding the dog. "We knew men failed to return," she said. "We
allowed ourselves to believe there were reasons." "There were," I told
her.

16
00:05:44,888 --> 00:06:05,847
"The nigga killed them." Orsini's face hardened. "You speak easily of
opposing him. You arrived with ships, friends, a fortune. Some of us
have been growing old beneath his windows." "I didn't arrive with
you," I said. "I earned you. Don't make that sound smaller because
you're scared now." He looked away. I let him.

17
00:06:06,097 --> 00:06:30,629
A man sometimes needs a minute to decide whether he hates the truth or
the person brave enough to say it in his courtyard. Bastien set
Eliane's letter on the table. Leonora recognized the handwriting. Her
hand went to her mouth. "She made my wedding gown." Bastien nodded.
"She also made sure someone remembered what happened at the harbor."
Marcellus showed them the ledger.

18
00:06:30,879 --> 00:06:55,616
No speech. No lecture. Just the pages and the names, the old promises
written beside sums large enough to have purchased several very
beautiful lies. Orsini sat down slowly. He found his brother's name. A
payment dated two days before the brother's ship disappeared. Leonora
put a hand on his shoulder. The old king read the line again. Then he
stood.

19
00:06:55,866 --> 00:07:14,124
"Rusk." "My lord." "Write the announcement." Nigga, sometimes courage
looks like an old man deciding his knees can complain later. We left
the courtyard with six signed house seals and the promise of more
before evening. Not because paper made people loyal.

20
00:07:14,374 --> 00:07:33,538
Because every man who signed had to look at the next man while doing
it, and some kinds of shame finally become useful when the room is
full enough. Drake waited outside in a black car. "The emperor
requests the original ledger." "The emperor can request better manners
while he's at it," I said.

21
00:07:33,788 --> 00:07:56,615
"You are building a funeral procession." "Nigga, you keep threatening
crowds that already saw me save them. Find a new hobby." He looked
past me at Rusk. "Your house has been searched." Rusk went pale. I
moved before Drake could enjoy it. One step. One hand on the car door.
One hard pull. The door opened with Drake still holding it.

22
00:07:56,865 --> 00:08:20,365
I dragged him out into the street and put him against the roof. His
guards reached for their guns. Ardent's officers, waiting behind us,
raised theirs first. Nigga, those were my niggas this morning. Every
one of them had watched Drake threaten their chief, and a nigga does
eventually get tired of seeing somebody disrespect the man who signs
his holiday leave.

23
00:08:20,615 --> 00:08:37,521
"Nobody," I said, "gets dramatic except me." Drake's face pressed
against black paint. "You have made a serious mistake." "Nigga, I
know. I should've bought this car in white. Shows bruises better." I
turned his face enough that he could see Rusk.

24
00:08:37,771 --> 00:09:00,240
"Where is his wife?" "At home." "Hurt?" "No." "Then you gonna call
your people and make sure that answer stays pretty." Drake looked at
the police, the crowd, the old king standing in his own gate with a
rifle he had clearly owned longer than Drake had been threatening
people. He called. I listened long enough to hear the men at Rusk's
house ordered away.

25
00:09:00,490 --> 00:09:20,751
Then I let him stand. "Tell Zero I accept the final," I said. "In
public. Crown on the stage. My people where I can see them." "And if
he refuses?" I looked around the street. At the faces in the windows.
At fourteen houses represented by men who had finally come outside
together.

26
00:09:21,001 --> 00:09:44,399
"Nigga, then we'll know which one of us is afraid of an audience." The
announcement went up at sunset. Rusk had written my name so large the
banner wouldn't fit through the opera house door. Tank had to carry it
out sideways while Rosa laughed from the steps. Across the city,
people stopped beneath balconies to hear it read. Final claim. Public
arena.

27
00:09:44,649 --> 00:10:06,804
Crown awarded before the houses and the city. No private coronation
required. Zero accepted an hour later. He had crossed out the word
captain before my name. Rusk put it back. Then he added a second line
beneath it. THE MAN WHO CAME WHEN WE CALLED. I looked at it for a long
time. Shawna came beside me.

28
00:10:07,054 --> 00:10:30,527
"You like that one?" "Nigga made it difficult to complain." "You can
manage." "The letters could be bigger." She laughed and slipped her
hand into mine. In the courtyard below, Rusk's wife arrived with a
little suitcase and kissed him hard enough to make the ceremonial
chain swing against his chest. Tank looked away respectfully. Rosa
looked directly at them and cheered.

29
00:10:30,777 --> 00:10:33,706
Nigga, both approaches had their virtues.
